        "summary":  "Anthropic consolidated Project Glasswing and its prior Cyber Verification Program into a unified three-tier framework granting security professionals graduated access to advanced Claude models including Opus 5.5 and Sonnet 5.5. Partners using Defense Access discovered approximately 129,000 software vulnerabilities between April and July 2026, with over 33,000 rated critical or high-severity. The tiered structure ranges from defensive security work to authorized penetration testing to critical infrastructure assessment, with the highest tier coordinated with U.S. government agencies.",
        "execSummary":  "Anthropic is actively expanding AI access for enterprise cybersecurity teams through a structured, government-coordinated program — a meaningful signal that frontier AI vendors are building trust frameworks for sensitive operational use. For enterprise security and IT leaders, this validates using advanced AI models in vulnerability management workflows, with documented productivity gains of months to years in threat detection velocity. The three-tier access model also establishes a governance template other vendors are likely to follow, making it a benchmark for how AI safety and enterprise utility can coexist. Leaders evaluating AI in security operations should monitor whether competitors match this framework, as it may become a procurement differentiator.",
        "vendorLean":  "Anthropic — promotes Anthropic\u0027s Claude models and safety programs",
