        "summary":  "Anthropic released Claude Sonnet 5.5, which scores 70.6% on Terminal-Bench 4.0 agentic coding versus Sonnet 5\u0027s 10.3%, while generating output 30% faster and costing up to 30% less per task due to reduced token consumption. The model runs at $2 per million input tokens and $10 per million output tokens — identical pricing to Sonnet 5 — but requires fewer tokens per task, translating to direct cost savings. Enterprise cybersecurity safeguards comparable to Opus 5.5 are included for the first time in the Sonnet line.",
        "execSummary":  "Sonnet 5.5 represents a step-change in the price-performance envelope for enterprise AI workloads: near-flagship capability at significantly lower operational cost, making it the practical default for high-volume applications like customer support ticket processing, financial analysis, and routine development tasks. For enterprise leaders evaluating AI cost structures, the 30% speed and efficiency gains compound at scale — a team running millions of interactions annually will see material budget impact without sacrificing output quality. The inclusion of Opus-level cybersecurity guardrails in Sonnet also removes a key objection to deploying the mid-tier model in security-sensitive contexts. The main caveat is that Sonnet 5.5\u0027s gains are concentrated in agentic coding and well-scoped tasks; complex open-ended strategic work still warrants Opus 5.5.",
