        "summary":  "This technical guide demonstrates how to build a personalized assistant called Sprout that retains conversational context across sessions using Amazon Bedrock\u0027s AgentCore runtime and memory capabilities combined with OpenClaw, an open-source agentic framework. The system accumulates and retrieves user-specific information to enable more contextual interactions. The complete architecture deploys via a single CloudFormation template on a consumption-based pricing model.",
        "execSummary":  "Enterprises evaluating persistent AI assistants now have a reference architecture combining AWS AgentCore and the open-source OpenClaw framework, deployable with a single CloudFormation template. The key advance is session-to-session memory: the agent accumulates user context over time rather than starting cold each conversation, which is the baseline requirement for any enterprise support or concierge use case. Leaders should note this is a fully AWS-managed stack, so switching costs are real — evaluate open-source memory alternatives before committing. The consumption-based pricing model suits variable workloads but warrants unit-cost modeling before scaling.",
