        "summary":  "This article explains how AWS helps organizations implement AI system impact assessments in accordance with the ISO/IEC 42005:2025 standard, integrating them into broader enterprise risk management processes. It outlines key guidance on documentation, lifecycle integration, and establishing repeatable assessment procedures. AWS shares its compliance tools and frameworks designed to support customers pursuing responsible AI governance aligned with international standards.",
        "execSummary":  "ISO/IEC 42005:2025 — the new international standard for AI system impact assessments — is now a compliance benchmark enterprises should be tracking, and AWS is positioning its tooling as the on-ramp. For enterprise leaders, the practical implication is that regulators and procurement teams will increasingly ask for documented impact assessments; having a repeatable, auditable process in place now reduces future fire drills. The AWS framing is helpful but vendor-specific — cross-reference against NIST AI RMF and EU AI Act obligations before treating AWS documentation as sufficient. Organizations in regulated industries should prioritize this standard in their AI governance roadmaps for 2027.",
