        "date":  "2026-10-05",
        "theme":  "Orchestration",
        "summary":  "This technical guide demonstrates how to implement retrieval-augmented generation (RAG) applications using Amazon Bedrock\u0027s managed knowledge bases with LangChain. The article compares standard single-query retrieval against agentic retrieval, which decomposes complex multi-part questions into sub-queries. The agentic approach improves recall on complex queries at the cost of higher per-call latency and expense.",
        "execSummary":  "Standard RAG pipelines fail on compound enterprise questions — agentic retrieval, which breaks queries into sub-queries before fetching context, materially improves answer quality on the complex, multi-part questions that dominate real enterprise workloads. AWS and LangChain now provide a managed, integrated path to deploy this pattern without custom orchestration code, lowering the barrier for enterprise teams. The trade-off is cost and latency: agentic retrieval is more expensive per call, so production deployments need query-routing logic to avoid applying it universally. Teams building internal knowledge assistants or customer-support bots should run a head-to-head benchmark on their own query distribution before committing to the pattern.",
