        "summary":  "Telecommunications operators are increasingly adopting open AI models to build customizable, trustworthy, and cost-effective AI workflows for critical operations. According to NVIDIA\u0027s latest telecommunications AI report, 89% of respondents consider open source models essential to their AI strategy. The article highlights five strategic advantages: lower costs, telco-specific customization, enhanced transparency for governance, flexible deployment options, and opportunities to deliver localized AI services to enterprise customers.",
        "execSummary":  "The telecom sector\u0027s near-universal pivot to open AI models is a leading indicator for enterprise AI broadly: proprietary frontier models are increasingly viewed as too expensive and too opaque for regulated, mission-critical workloads. The 89% adoption signal from NVIDIA\u0027s survey is vendor-commissioned but directionally consistent with broader market trends, so treat it as a floor rather than a precise figure. For enterprise AI leaders outside telecom, the five strategic advantages cited — cost, customization, transparency, deployment flexibility, and service monetization — map directly to the evaluation criteria for any industry vertical considering open versus closed model strategies. The caveat: open models require significantly more internal MLOps capability to operationalize safely than SaaS-wrapped proprietary alternatives.",
