        "date":  "2026-10-06",
        "theme":  "Strategy",
        "summary":  "Evident\u0027s annual AI index finds major banks are significantly accelerating responsible AI adoption and governance frameworks as they scale deployments. Nearly all surveyed financial institutions now have responsible AI principles in place, with JPMorgan Chase and Capital One leading in maturity metrics. Institutions are investing heavily in specialized talent and implementing strict controls to mitigate risks in the highly regulated environment.",
        "execSummary":  "Banking sector AI governance has shifted from aspirational policy to operational execution, with virtually all major institutions now running structured responsible AI programs — a meaningful signal for other regulated industries. JPMorgan and Capital One are emerging as benchmarks, having moved beyond principles documents to measurable governance frameworks with dedicated talent. The implication for enterprise leaders: governance maturity is becoming a competitive differentiator, not just a compliance checkbox. If your AI program lacks a documented responsible AI framework with named accountability, you are behind the emerging peer standard.",
        "vendorLean":  "Evident — article frames findings through Evident\u0027s AI governance analytics platform and features its co-CEO prominently",
