        "date":  "2026-10-05",
        "theme":  "Enterprise",
        "summary":  "Schneider Electric developed a four-tier AI training program in partnership with Coursera to address enterprise skills gaps that block successful adoption, tailoring instruction for four groups: all 160,000 workers, executives, software engineers, and transformation leads. The company emphasizes cross-functional teams and practical application, with mandatory foundational training as the baseline. CEO Philippe Rambach acknowledges that \u0027we are all learning\u0027 as organizations navigate the deployment challenge.",
        "execSummary":  "Schneider Electric\u0027s tiered AI literacy program — mandatory for all 160,000 employees, with specialized tracks for executives and engineers — represents an operationally mature approach to the skills gap that stalls most enterprise AI programs. The key insight is that undifferentiated training fails; role-specific curricula with practical application exercises is what drives adoption. For enterprise leaders, the Schneider model is a deployable blueprint: start with a universal baseline, then layer role-specific depth, and partner with an established learning platform rather than building curriculum from scratch. The bottleneck is organizational will, not available content.",
